# Fly Launch generated a one-line .dockerignore alongside a `COPY . /srv/http/`
# static-server Dockerfile. That combination publishes the entire build context
# as downloadable files. Secrets first, everything else after.
#
# This still matters with the current Node/Hono Dockerfile: its build stage
# runs `COPY . .` into the image before `npm run build`, so anything not
# excluded here is available to be copied forward into the runtime stage (or
# read during the build) even though the runtime stage only explicitly
# copies a short allow-list of paths back out. Every rule below still applies.

# Secrets — never in a build context, under any circumstances
.env
.env.*
*.local
# ...except the checked-in templates (.env.example, .env.local.example),
# which carry no values and document what to set, not a secret to hide.
!*.example

# Version control history
.git
.gitignore

# Dependencies and build output (installed/built inside the image)
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
dev-dist
**/dev-dist

# Tooling and scratch
.superpowers
.claude
.vscode
.idea
coverage
*.log

# Docs and plans — no reason to ship them
docs
README.md

# Fly's own config
fly.toml
.dockerignore
